{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And you shall teach them diligently to your children</b>. These too are explained commandments already hinted at, for since He commanded in the commandments — 'a perpetual statute throughout your generations, a sign between Me and the children of Israel forever' (Exodus 31:17), 'this is My covenant which you shall keep between Me and you and your seed after you' (Genesis 17:10) — behold, we are commanded that our children should know the commandments, and how will they know them if we do not teach them? And likewise, 'And you shall bind them for a sign upon your hand, and they shall be for frontlets between your eyes' was already stated (Exodus 13:9), and here He explained <b>and you shall bind them</b>, that they should be placed bound, and it alludes as well to the knot of tefillin that our Rabbis received as a halachah le-Moshe mi-Sinai (Menachot 35a). And He added here the commandment of the mezuzah — 'And you shall write them on the doorposts of your house and on your gates' — which was not mentioned; and perhaps this too is an explained matter hinted there in the commandment of 'and for a memorial between your eyes, so that the Torah of HaShem may be in your mouth.' And the sense of <b>and on your gates</b> is: and on the doorposts of your other gates, such as the gates of cities and provinces, as in 'within one of your gates' (Deuteronomy 15:7)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "The phrase 'placed bound' translates מונחים בקשירה, which may refer specifically to the physical tying/knotting of tefillin; rendered literally to preserve Ramban's play on the root ק-ש-ר."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:46:06.146850809Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}